# --- Secrets: never commit ---
# The prod deployment keeps every live secret in a .env file (SAFETY-RULES),
# and this repo previously leaked three real secrets into git history.
# These entries make a stray `git add -A` incapable of repeating that.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Contains a prod IP, an SSH key path and a `curl -u "$SOURCE_USERNAME:$SOURCE_PASSWORD"`
# command. Until now it was only excluded by the developer's GLOBAL gitignore,
# so a fresh clone on another machine would have committed it.
.claude/settings.local.json